    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d155">

                <pb facs="0545" n="425" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg425"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">813.00 Tacoma/–: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Ramer</hi>)<anchor n="49"
                        xml:id="d155-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-25T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 25,
                                1922—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>33. You will transmit to President Chamorro the following message from the
                    President: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“It is with great satisfaction and gratification that I learn that Your
                            Excellency was enabled by the meeting on board the U. S. S. <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Tacoma</hi> to arrive at an agreement with the
                            Presidents of El Salvador and Honduras with a view to maintaining
                            amicable fraternal relations of good will and peace among your
                            countries. It was a great pleasure to be able to assist this conference
                            in any way, and I <pb facs="0546" n="426" xml:id="pg426"/> assure you of
                            the continued interest of the United States Government and people, as
                            well as my own personal interest in the welfare of your country. Warren
                            G. Harding.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d155-f1" n="49" type="source" xml:id="d155-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, to the Ministers in
                    Honduras (no. 31) and Salvador (no. 42).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
